    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Pirate Face Rescues LLM Models from Deletion",
      "url": "https://pirateface.co/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49776699",
      "score": 537,
      "comments": 143,
      "author": "skepticalgenius",
      "published": "2026-09-20T15:16:07Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Centralized hubs like Hugging Face risk model disappearance from DMCA takedowns, licensing shifts, and author deletions, threatening research reproducibility.",
        "Pirate Face archives threatened open-weights LLMs using BitTorrent and decentralized storage, ensuring permanent access to deprecated or censored checkpoints.",
        "Production pipelines relying on upstream hub URLs need self-hosted artifact registries or torrent-backed mirrors to mitigate sudden dependency loss."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Software sandboxing: The basics (2025)",
      "url": "https://blog.emilua.org/2025/01/12/software-sandboxing-basics/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/brptxb",
      "score": 43,
      "comments": 19,
      "author": "vinipsmaker",
      "published": "2026-09-20T14:13:11Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Linux sandboxing relies on seccomp-bpf for syscall filtering, alongside namespaces, cgroups, and Landlock LSM for fine-grained process isolation.",
        "Modern implementations increasingly favor WebAssembly (WASI) runtimes or microVMs like Firecracker over traditional chroots to safely isolate untrusted workloads.",
        "Effective sandboxing balances kernel attack surface reduction against IPC serialization overhead, filesystem broker complexity, and privilege separation boundaries."
      ]
    },
